---
description: Side-by-side form controls must have the same size
globs: src/**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---

# Matching control sizes

Controls placed next to each other (in the same row or grid row) must render at the same
height and visual weight: dropdown next to text box, input next to button, etc.

- Single-line `<input>` and `<select>` use `fieldClass` from `src/components/ui/field.ts`
  (explicit `h-9`). Never size them with vertical padding alone: the Tauri WebKit webview
  ignores `py-*` on native selects, so they end up thinner than inputs.
- `<textarea>` uses `textAreaClass`.
- Buttons beside a field in the same row match the field height (`h-9`).
- Controls in the same grid row also share width rules (`w-full` in equal columns), and
  labels above them use the same text style so the fields line up.
- When adding a new control style, update `field.ts` rather than inlining one-off classes.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD: select renders shorter than the input next to it
<select className="rounded-md border px-2 py-1.5" />
<input className="rounded-md border px-2 py-1.5" />

// ✅ GOOD
<select className={fieldClass} />
<input className={fieldClass} />
```
